rt to the evasion of  the innate immune system depletion of  drp1 our parking induced robust  cytochrome C release from the  mitochondria and promoted activation of  Casa page 37 followed by subsequent  cleavage of poly adp-ribose polymerase a  casa base substrate induction of  apoptosis was also substantiated by  tunel assay which shows accumulation of  tunel-positive cells together these  results strongly suggest that hcv  mediated induction of mitochondrial  fission and mitophagy although serving  as a quality control mechanism to  eliminate damaged mitochondria also  protects wireless infected hepatocytes  from apoptotic cell death facilitating  persistent viral infection next we will  talk about an interesting paper from  dang Lee's lab published in cell stem  cell the paper talks about human somatic  cell nuclear transfer using adult cells  successful somatic cell nuclear transfer  that is a CNT with human cells has  proved to be challenging to achieve only  fetal or infant scnt has been reported  so far authors generated human embryonic  stem cells via Sen T using dermal  fibroblasts from 35 and 75 year old  males embryonic stem cells expressed  standard stem cell markers genetic  analysis revealed that nuclear DNA  derived from male donor and  mitochondrial DNA  derived from both sides now we can  generate human embryonic stem cells  directly from adults next we will look  into an interesting paper from paola or  Lotus lab published in science Milan is  implicated in complex neuronal function  including learning and cognition and  abnormal myelination is associated with  neurological disorders conductance of  neural signals depending depend on  thickness of the myelin the distribution  of myelinated tracks along the length of  action has been assumed to be uniform  authors looked at the Milan distribution  along single axons in the murine brain  using sophisticated high-throughput  electron microscopy what they found out  was individual neurons have distinct